Reproduced offline (bug hunt 2026-09-26).

lib/Langertha/Role/Chat.pm:263 _normalize_content_blocks returns the message unchanged unless it holds a Langertha::Content object (gemini excepted). For content_format "ollama" an OpenAI-style array of text parts therefore goes out verbatim:
  $o->chat_request($o->chat_messages({role=>"user", content=>[{type=>"text",text=>"hi"}]}))
  -> {"messages":[{"content":[{"text":"hi","type":"text"}],"role":"user"}],...}
Native /api/chat Message.content is a string (api/types.go); the server answers 400 (cannot unmarshal array into string). The ollama branch (lines ~272-290) already flattens text parts and would croak with a clear message on unknown parts, but it is never reached without a Content object. Gateways forwarding OpenAI-shape messages hit this.

Fix: treat fmt eq "ollama" like gemini in the early return (always run the ollama branch for an ARRAY content); decide whether an {type=>"image_url"} hash part is converted through Content::Image (as _gemini_part does) or croaks. Request-building test in t/2x.
